sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-10> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Speed varies as the square root of linear size in swimming, flight and walking (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "Minimum flight speed under isometry and speed at equal Froude number both scale as the square root of the linear dimension." ;
    dct:source "On Growth and Form (1917)" ;
    skos:notation "V \\propto L^{1/2} for swimming (Froude), flight (minimum speed) and walking (pendulum leg)" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **R4, conclusion 2.** Under R1, R2 and the same `ρ`, `C_L,max` for every member, `v_min` scales as `√L`. -/
theorem vmin_ratio {W S : ℝ → ℝ} {k₁ k₂ ρ Cmax : ℝ} (hW : CubeLaw W k₁) (hS : AreaLaw S k₂) (hρ : 0 < ρ)
    (hCmax : 0 < Cmax) {L₁ L₂ : ℝ} (h₁ : 0 < L₁) (h₂ : 0 < L₂) :
    vmin ρ Cmax (W L₂) (S L₂) / vmin ρ Cmax (W L₁) (S L₁) = Real.sqrt (L₂ / L₁)"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.froudeSpeed" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.vmin_ratio", "Delphi.froude_ratio" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Two of Thompson's three routes: flight (v_min ∝ L^(1/2) under R1, R2, constant ρ and C_L,max) and swimming (Froude: v ∝ (g L)^(1/2) at equal Froude number). The walking (pendulum) route is not formalised." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-10> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-10> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch02-10> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch02-10> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.vmin_ratio with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 2 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.5 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean (254 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.vmin_ratio, Delphi.froude_ratio: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T19:09:31.039Z): 2 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [scaling-vmin-exponent-one] R4 scaling mutant: v_min claimed to scale as L (exponent 1) instead of sqrt(L). Rejected with 3 error(s): scaling-vmin-exponent-one.lean:151:71: error: unsolved goals [scaling-froude-exponent-one] R8 mutant: Froude speed claimed to scale as L instead of sqrt(L). Rejected with 1 error(s): scaling-froude-exponent-one.lean:247:59: error: unsolved goals Controls: 11 of 11 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-10> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

